(the reaped status after a child is killed by a signal. The parent
 forks a child that sleeps, sends SIGKILL, reaps (blocking), and decodes
 the raw status word: signal 9, crashed true, exited normally false,
 exit code 0. The other half of the lib/process.vox coverage - the true
 states of crashed and signal and the false state of exited normally,
 all against a real child.)

see "../lib/process.vox".

Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Wait 30 seconds.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    Send signal 9 to process pid,
    Set 'reaped pid' to reap child pid,
    Set status to the reaped status,
    Print "reaped pid matches: {'reaped pid' is pid}",
    Print "signal: {'signal of' of status}",
    Print "crashed: {crashed of status}",
    Print "exited normally: {'exited normally' of status}",
    Print "exit code: {'exit code of' of status}".